function generateComplianceDraft(): Array<{ kind: string; title: string; body: string; channel: string | null; metadata: string }> {
  return [{
    kind: 'compliance', title: 'Responsible AI Statement (300-500 words)',
    channel: null,
    body: `## Compliance & Responsible AI Statement

### Privacy & Data Protection
FreeLeased processes lease and contract documents — never biometric, emotional, or behavioral data about individuals. All analysis is document-only: clauses are scored against statutory floors, never people against norms. The platform operates under a privacy-by-design model: resident PII is scrubbed by the Redaction Protocol before any dossier reaches the consensus gate, and the Cryptographic Communes layer enforces k-anonymity (≥5) before any aggregate data is surfaced.

### Bias & Fairness
The fairness engine scores lease clauses against statute — it does not profile tenants or landlords. Each fairness check carries an evidence class (established/heuristic/contested/unfalsifiable) that caps the displayed confidence. Advisory results are explicitly labeled as such. The system never makes automated decisions about individuals; it produces advisory outputs that require human sign-off (HITL) before any action is taken.

### Safety & Prohibited Practices
FreeLeased does not engage in: subliminal manipulation, exploitation of vulnerabilities, social scoring, emotion recognition, biometric categorization, or predictive profiling. The platform's "adversary intelligence" layer (retired from active use per CoC compliance review) was designed strictly for defensive analysis of manipulation patterns in legal language — not for profiling individuals or groups. It has been scoped down to transparent, HITL-gated defensive-only functionality.

### Transparency & Human Oversight
All AI-generated content carries provenance markers. The consensus gate requires 2/3 human validation before any claim surfaces as "verified." The system's confidence levels are bounded by evidence class, and uncertain results are flagged for human review rather than presented as authoritative. Residents retain full opt-out capability and can revoke consent at any point in the workflow.

### Synthetic Content & Disclosure
All AI-generated text within FreeLeased is marked as synthetic. When the platform interacts with users, it discloses its AI nature. Audit trails are immutable and available for inspection.

### License & Open Source
FreeLeased will be released under a permissive open-source license, enabling community audit and adaptation across jurisdictions.

### Limitations
This is a Level 4→5 prototype. Statutory data is based on verified primary sources for pilot jurisdictions, but coverage is not yet comprehensive. Caribbean adaptations are based on structural analogies with UK law — they require in-territory legal review before deployment. The platform is advisory, not a substitute for legal counsel.`,
    metadata: JSON.stringify({ wordCount: 420, section: 'compliance', coCSections: ['§2', '§3', '§4', '§5'] }),
  }]
}

// Generate content drafts — idempotent (won't duplicate existing drafts by title).
app.post('/competition/generate', async (c) => {
  const body = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}))
  const kind: string = body?.kind ?? 'all'

  let drafts: Array<{ kind: string; title: string; body: string; channel: string | null; metadata: string }> = []
  if (kind === 'social' || kind === 'all') drafts.push(...generateSocialDrafts())
  if (kind === 'journal' || kind === 'all') drafts.push(...generateJournalDraft())
  if (kind === 'compliance' || kind === 'all') drafts.push(...generateComplianceDraft())
  if (kind === 'overview' || kind === 'all') {
    // Overview doc: auto-generated from current state
    const stats = {
      statutes: STATUTES.length, sources: SOURCES.length,
      jurisdictions: JURISDICTIONS.length, patterns: HIDDEN_RIGHTS.length,
    }
    drafts.push({
      kind: 'overview', title: 'Project Overview (auto-generated)',
      channel: null,
      body: `## FreeLeased — Project Overview\n\n**Problem:** 4M+ UK leaseholders struggle to exercise statutory rights (RTM, enfranchisement, service-charge audit). Caribbean jurisdictions have no digital leasehold governance tools.\n\n**Solution:** Open-source, local-first, resident-led platform that automates statutory diagnostics. Data spine: ${stats.jurisdictions} jurisdictions, ${stats.statutes} statutes, ${stats.sources} verified sources, ${stats.patterns} hidden-rights patterns.\n\n**Architecture:** Codified-first (deterministic code) with RAG-agentic fallback (LLM only for genuinely ambiguous claims). Consensus gate requires 2/3 human validation. Veracity engine scores every claim by evidence class.\n\n**Differentiators:**\n- $0 compute spend — local SQLite, deterministic code\n- Provenance chain — every claim traceable to primary source\n- Jurisdiction-agnostic spine — 9 jurisdictions mapped, globally scalable\n- HITL by design — resident-led, not AI-led\n\n**Business Model:** Freemium SaaS. Free tier for individual leaseholders. Premium for property managers. Enterprise for housing associations. Caribbean licensing via MoU partnerships.\n\n**Current TRL:** Level 4→5 (working prototype, first real-user test in progress).`,
      metadata: JSON.stringify({ stats }),
    })
  }

  // Deduplicate by title
  const existingTitles = new Set(
    (await prisma.contentDraft.findMany({ select: { title: true } })).map((d) => d.title)
  )
  const newDrafts = drafts.filter((d) => !existingTitles.has(d.title))
  if (newDrafts.length > 0) {
    await prisma.contentDraft.createMany({ data: newDrafts })
  }
  return c.json({ ok: true, generated: newDrafts.length, skipped: drafts.length - newDrafts.length })
})

